From 176a535473933473feb77449870264d01ee30293 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: freakymustard67 <freakymustard67@://github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 07:06:37 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] semantics: project approach goals to free space; never
 splice a blocked goal (w4b F1/F2)

- Planner.project_to_free(): the free_near substitute as a public projection;
  run.py --find uses it so the latch and metrics target a reachable point (F1).
- Planner.plan() no longer splices a blocked goal onto the path: the final
  waypoint stays the free substitute, so path_valid/path_bearing_deg cannot
  advertise a point the planner itself blocks (F2).
- config: DestinationConfig standoff documented and validated against the
  geometric floor (inflation + cell + margin); RoomConfig.required_standoff_m()
  encodes the per-object rule (>= obj_r + 0.35 with the shipped constants).
- tests/test_approach_standoff.py pins no-splice, projection consistency,
  the standoff rule and the validation floor.
